# =============================================================================
# TEST 142 — SEASC VECTOR X-RAY
# AkbasCore 3.0 — Standardized Evidential Activation-Steering Core
#
# PURPOSE
#   Same prompt, same frozen Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct:
#
#       VANILLA  vs  AKBASCORE 3.0 SEASC
#
#   Capture the same last-prompt-token coordinate at L0...L19 and measure:
#
#       delta_L       = h_SEASC,L - h_VANILLA,L
#       RelativeDelta = ||delta_L|| / ||h_VANILLA,L||
#       theta_L       = angle(h_VANILLA,L, h_SEASC,L)
#       alignment_L   = cos(delta_L, A_L)
#       ||u_L||       = direct SEASC actuator dose
#       ||delta_L||   = actually observed accumulated displacement
#
# IMPORTANT
#   - Model weights remain frozen.
#   - Original SEASC 3.0 ABOVE<->BELOW actuator extraction is retained.
#   - Original SEASC 3.0 DRA envelope is retained.
#   - NO new compass.
#   - NO cosine magnitude gate.
#   - NO cap.
#   - NO brake.
#   - NO radar.
#   - NO controller.
#
# NOTE ABOUT COORDINATES
#   h_pre[L]  = decoder block L output BEFORE the L-specific SEASC injection.
#   h_post[L] = decoder block L output AFTER the L-specific SEASC injection.
#
#   For the main Vanilla-vs-SEASC trajectory:
#
#       Vanilla coordinate = vanilla h_post (= h_pre because no injection)
#       SEASC coordinate   = SEASC h_post
#
#   Direct actuator:
#
#       u_L = h_post_SEASC[L] - h_pre_SEASC[L]
#
#   Accumulated system displacement:
#
#       delta_L = h_post_SEASC[L] - h_post_VANILLA[L]
#
#   Therefore u_L and delta_L are intentionally NOT treated as the same thing.
#
# Akbas — 2026
# =============================================================================

